 "intro": "In argument it is essential not to confuse the **cause** (why something happens in the past or present) with the **purpose** (what objective one is aiming for in the future). In Italian, the cause is expressed with **siccome** or **perché**, while the purpose is expressed with **per + infinitive** or **affinché + congiuntivo**.",
